Integer fog for 8-bit colour spans

_swrast_fog_rgba_span blended every pixel in floats: a division by w,
three byte-to-float and three float-to-byte conversions and, with
GL_NICEST, an expf(). For spans of 8-bit colours with an interpolated
fog coordinate (all triangles) the pixel is now blended as one 32-bit
word in integers, with the fog factor as 0..256. With per-vertex fog
(the default fog hint) the factor is worked out exactly every 8 pixels
and linearly in between; with GL_NICEST it is still worked out for
every pixel. Pictures differ from before by at most 1 in a channel;
alpha is unchanged. Asked for by the YSFlight port (fogged sky and
ground, 15-17% of a frame in _swrast_fog_rgba_span); checked by
tests/host-harness/mesa/render-fog.

